**Reproduced:** `strace -f -e trace=openat ./target/debug/rb test | grep tests/` showed `rb test` opening `tests/redblue_test.rs` and `tests/expect_test.rs` — Rust source fed to the Redblue harness. (The prompt's stronger "reported as a failure" no longer reproduces on `c4ebad3`; phase-001's `// test ` marker requirement suppressed the symptom, but the `.rs` reads were still happening. Recorded honestly in REPORT.md.)

**Fix:** `src/testing/mod.rs` — `find_test_files` now collects only `ext == "rb"`; `run_all_tests` drops the redundant extension guard. +204/−5 in one file.

**Tests:** 8 new `#[test]` in `src/testing/mod.rs`, 4 of which failed first for the right reason. 5 named `edge_*`; `edge_non_utf8_rb_file_reports_read_error` asserts an `Error::Io`. Zero ignores/skips.

**Gates:** `cargo fmt --check` pass · `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` pass, zero warnings · `cargo test --all-targets` 39 passed / 0 failed · `./rbops/verify.sh` **not run — `rbops/` does not exist in this checkout**, so substitutes were run instead: `rb test` 22 run / 21 passed / 0 failed, all 6 `examples/*.rb` exit 0. `modules/MathUtils.rb` errors identically before and after my change (verified via `git stash`) — pre-existing, in FINDINGS.md.

`phases/phase-002/REPORT.md` and `FINDINGS.md` written. Nothing under `.github/`, `rbops/`, or `.opencode/agent/` touched; not committed.
